eering. Source: `.../2026-09-30-strategic-digest.md`.\n\n**Things to check before this goes to Mateo**\n- **#8841 history doesn't line up.** The ticket is described as open in May, closed on 1 Jul, then submitted by Mateo on 30 Sep. The Allentown and Newark descriptions also differ. It could be a reused number or a reopened ticket. I can't tell from what I can see, so Gideon should confirm against the support system.\n- **Possible extra ticket, #PD-4418.** The 15 Sep 2025 digest has \"the account Nadia runs\" with a warehouse supervisor reporting the `Carrier_Dwell_Summary` export dropping timestamps at Dock Door 9. It never names the account, and Nadia runs several. I've left it off the list. Please confirm it's Vantorre Group before it goes in. Source: `.../2025-09-15-strategic-digest.md`.\n- **Excluded as not the parent:** #4812 is Vantorre Mobility (3/10/2025 digest), and #PD-4402 is Quillfeather.\n- **No ticket number anywhere:** the 3 Aug 2026 digest and the 3/10/2025 gate-delay email from Mateo.\n- **Moss's other digests** (7/7/2025, 12/1/2025, 5/3/2026 and the cheat sheet) have no Vantorre Group ticket numbers.\n- **I only checked the three sources you named.** I haven't looked at the account's ticket files or support system, so this is the full history from those sources only, not necessarily the complete ticket history."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
